# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > l+ l- j at LO (default coupling orders).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The default-order half of the llj pair. One extra QCD coupling for the
#     jet takes the order selection past the trivial case, so this and
#     pp_to_llj_qcd2_qed2 together pin what "default orders" means once more
#     than one power of a coupling is in play: the two must select the same
#     diagram content, and a change to the selector that broke that would show
#     up as one count moving.
#   - Its run card takes MadGraph's dynamical scale choice, which the scale
#     layer refuses rather than approximates (a 2 -> 3 needs general kT
#     clustering for the cluster scale). That refusal is itself asserted, so
#     this row is the negative case of the scale gate: a scale we decline to
#     claim, stated as such rather than left untested.
#
# Not used for cross sections or event samples: the refusal above blocks them.
# pp_to_llj_fixed has the same generate line with all three scales fixed at m_Z,
# and it is the integrals, samples and event-generation subject of the triple.
generate p p > l+ l- j
output pp_to_llj -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  done
